  "rewrites": {
   "6": {
    "original": "There is plenty of passenger ergonomics - you\u2019ll struggle to find much fault as to the Yeti\u2019s interior, particularly with the B&O sound system displaying good quality bass notes and a blowsy mid-range sound.",
    "rewrite": "The interior is well-designed in terms of passenger comfort; you will hardly find any complaints about the Yeti\u2019s cabin, especially regarding the high-quality bass and vibrant mid-range sound from the B&O system."
   },
   "12": {
    "original": "There\u2019s a lot of relaxed work available with the Yeti and the dynamic models only offer a slightly perverse and awkward car that needs some serious coaxing to return to secure, predictable and safe handling.",
    "rewrite": "There is a significant amount of laid-back work available with the Yeti, while the dynamic models provide a somewhat odd and challenging driving experience that lacks predictability and security."
   },
   "3": {
    "original": "In the boot the cube shape is highlighted by the prominent tribes on the carpet and there\u2019s a wide range of small storage options, and space to house a wheelchair in two of the full size, split seats.",
    "rewrite": "The boot stands out for its cube design, marked by noticeable patterns on the carpet, with a variety of small storage choices, and enough space in two full-size, divided seats to accommodate a wheelchair."
   },
   "10": {
    "original": "True, you\u2019re never likely to be seriously off roofing or rock climbing in a Yeti and a lot of the excess unladen weight makes most of its 640kg mass a simple, if slightly noisy, companion.",
    "rewrite": "It's true that you're rarely in danger of encountering a Yeti while roof surfing or rock climbing, and much of its 640kg unladen weight is simply extra, though not necessarily cumbersome or overly disruptive."
   },
   "5": {
    "original": "This will probably suit many buyers although personal music players and Blackberrys will probably not be able to be used simply throughuetooth three or through a plug socket.",
    "rewrite": "This is likely to suit many buyers, though personal music players and Blackberrys may not be usable through Bluetooth or by plugging them in."
   },
   "9": {
    "original": "Combine that with a high centre of gravity when it comes to the optional four-wheel drive models and you\u2019ve got some sportiness supressed off road.",
    "rewrite": "Adding to that, the optional four-wheel drive models have a high centre of gravity, which suppresses the sporty handling off-road."
   },
   "8": {
    "original": "The soft, damp ride and prominent high wring roar at high speeds can get wearing quickly, although with city cruising its a different story.",
    "rewrite": "The gentle, moist ride and obvious loud wail at high speeds can become tiresome fast, though for city driving it's a contrasting experience."
   },
   "11": {
    "original": "What you do find is the hallmarks of German engineering and this is highlighted in the well judged four-wheel drive models.",
    "rewrite": "The hallmark of German engineering is evident in what you discover, particularly in the well-judged four-wheel drive models."
   },
   "4": {
    "original": "Skoda seems to have chosen buttons and dials over the latest technology for the Yeti.",
    "rewrite": "It appears that Skoda favored buttons and dials over the latest technology in the Yeti."
   },
   "13": {
    "original": "Skoda Yeti road test - 4x4 car review - Which compact 4x4 car is best?",
    "rewrite": "Which compact 4x4 car emerged as the best in the Skoda Yeti road test and 4x4 car review?"
   },
   "14": {
    "original": "Skoda Yeti 2.0 TDI - 4x4 car review - Which compact 4x4 car is best?",
    "rewrite": "Review of the Skoda Yeti 2.0 TDI 4x4 - Which small 4x4 car stands out as the best?"
   },
   "1": {
    "original": "There\u2019s certainly no lack of leg room for the driver and their passenger but space is very tight behind the front seats.",
    "rewrite": "There isn't any shortage of space for the driver and their passenger, but the rear seating area is quite cramped."
   }
  },
  "final_span": "tilted or rotated or folded out of the way to provide more cargo carrying space.\nThere isn't any shortage of space for the driver and their passenger, but the rear seating area is quite cramped.\nSkoda Yeti goes for an off-roading feel\nThe boot stands out for its cube design, marked by noticeable patterns on the carpet, with a variety of small storage choices, and enough space in two full-size, divided seats to accommodate a wheelchair.\nIt appears that Skoda favored buttons and dials over the latest technology in the Yeti. This is likely to suit many buyers, though personal music players and Blackberrys may not be usable through Bluetooth or by plugging them in.\nThe interior is well-designed in terms of passenger comfort; you will hardly find any complaints about the Yeti\u2019s cabin, especially regarding the high-quality bass and vibrant mid-range sound from the B&O system.\nIf there is one issue the Yeti does not shake off readily it is its very noisy ride. The gentle, moist ride and obvious loud wail at high speeds can become tiresome fast, though for city driving it's a contrasting experience.\nAdding to that, the optional four-wheel drive models have a high centre of gravity, which suppresses the sporty handling off-road.\nIt's true that you're rarely in danger of encountering a Yeti while roof surfing or rock climbing, and much of its 640kg unladen weight is simply extra, though not necessarily cumbersome or overly disruptive.\nThe hallmark of German engineering is evident in what you discover, particularly in the well-judged four-wheel drive models.\nThere is a significant amount of laid-back work available with the Yeti, while the dynamic models provide a somewhat odd and challenging driving experience that lacks predictability and security.\nWhich compact 4x4 car emerged as the best in the Skoda Yeti road test and 4x4 car review?\nReview of the Skoda Yeti 2.0 TDI 4x4 - Which small 4x4 car stands out as the best?\nOverall the Yeti offers a touch of class to a market rarely associated",
  "break_point": {
